    "body": "## Summary\n\n`RotaryEmbedding.forward_xpu()`'s fallback-kernel branch (used when `head_size` is not in `[128, 256, 512]`) calls `torch.ops.sgl_kernel.rotary_embedding(positions, query, key, self.head_size, self.cos_sin_cache, self.is_neox_style)` without slicing to `rotary_dim` first. That compiled kernel asserts `rotary_dim == head_size` internally and raises:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: Rotary dim doesn't match query head_size\n```\n\nfor any model with partial rotary embeddings (`rotary_dim < head_size`). This affects GPT-NeoX-style architectures with `partial_rotary_factor < 1.0` on XPU (e.g. `adept/persimmon-8b-chat`, `microsoft/phi-2`, `stabilityai/stablelm-2-1_6b`, `stabilityai/stablelm-3b-4e1t`, `stabilityai/stablelm-zephyr-3b`), independent of the `--attention-backend` choice (`triton` or `intel_xpu`), since rotary embedding dispatch is keyed on device type (`is_xpu()`), not attention backend.\n\nThe fix adds an `elif self.head_size != self.rotary_dim` branch that falls back to `forward_native()`, which already implements generic partial-rotary math correctly (splitting `query[..., :self.rotary_dim]` / `query[..., self.rotary_dim:]`). This mirrors the existing pattern where `forward_cpu`/`forward_npu` already fall back to `forward_native` for their own unsupported cases, and the aligned-head_size branch of `forward_xpu` itself already slices to `rotary_dim` before its fused call.\n\n## Test plan\n\nHardware-validated on Intel XPU with the patched build, running a 20-example accuracy smoke check per model (server + client, real GPU):\n- `adept/persimmon-8b-chat` (intel_xpu backend, gsm8k) — passed, no crash\n- `microsoft/phi-2` (triton backend, gsm8k) — passed, no crash\n- `stabilityai/stablelm-3b-4e1t` (triton backend, hellaswag) — passed, no crash\n- `stabilityai/stablelm-zephyr-3b` (triton backend, gsm8k) — passed, no crash\n\nAll four previously failed with `RuntimeError: Rotary dim doesn't match query head_size` on this code path; all four now serve and produce results after the fix. `stabilityai/stablelm-2-1_6b` hits the same root cause and is also fixed by this change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35979999957](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35979999957)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35979999378](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35979999378)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35979999968](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35979999968)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
